From ce84bda6957e9336f601e5c2f181e0fc806229d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kulesha Evgeniy <voovdop@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:27:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/29] turnip/a5xx: CPU paths for buffer/image ops, skip GPU
 barriers

The a5xx sysmem driver cannot use the common r2d blit engine or the
a6xx cache-flush packets: vkCmdFillBuffer/vkCmdUpdateBuffer/
vkCmdCopyBuffer2/vkCmdCopyImage2/vkCmdClearColorImage and the
buffer<->image copies are now done on the CPU (memcpy/memset) with
explicit cache maintenance, matching the existing host-image-copy
helpers. Barriers are a no-op on chip 5; emitting the a6xx flush
sequence from vkCmdPipelineBarrier hangs the GPU.
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_clear_blit.cc | 408 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc |   8 +
 2 files changed, 407 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_clear_blit.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_clear_blit.cc
